# --- sense markers and punctuation ---------------------------------------
# Markers have to come from the subset of Unicode that ordinary body fonts
# actually cover, or they render as missing-glyph boxes.  Helvetica, Times and
# the macOS system font have no U+25AA/U+25AB, and U+25B8 is absent from every
# font checked except SF -- so the obvious squares-and-triangle set is exactly
# the wrong choice.  These three are in Mac Roman, cp1252 and WGL4, i.e. as
# safe as ASCII, and still give three distinct nesting levels.
14	•	sense
32	•
4440	•
21	›	sub-sense
24	◊	sub-sub-sense
282	…
1484	…
50	—
169	—
432	—
434	—
828	—
169,169	—	doubled to make a long dash
432,432	—
434,434	—
828,828	—
202	−	superscript minus, in chemical formulae
204	–	bond dash

